teasomal degradation of target proteins including CTNNB1, FOXA2 and AKT1 (PubMed:35768649, PubMed:37875418, PubMed:41323265). Involved in chromosome segregation and cell cycle regulation (PubMed:28087737). May play a role in the acrosome reaction and fertilization. Inhibits lung fibroblast proliferation, migration, and differentiation. Mechanistically, mediates 'Lys-48'-linked polyubiquitination of phospho-AKT1, leading to its proteasomal degradation and consequent inhibition of AKT signaling (PubMed:41323265). Promotes apoptosis via inhibition of the Wnt/beta-catenin signaling pathway (PubMed:35768649). Regulates ferroptosis by ubiquitinating and degrading FOXA2 (PubMed:37875418)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}